From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:02:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the /btw answer is drawn at the thread's text size

Operator ask of 2026-11-23 (item 6, second half): the /btw answer did not
look like the thread's answers, and nobody could say what differed. An Xvfb
proof with the same Markdown in both places measured it on 2026-11-24: same
family and the same 25 px line pitch, but the /btw text 14.2 % wider -- 16 px
against the thread's 14 px at the default sizes, and still 8/7 with
agent_ui_font_size at 20.

Both go through ThreadView::render_markdown with
MarkdownStyle::themed(MarkdownFont::Agent), and that style sets no size on
its container: the Markdown's text takes the size of the element around it.
Each assistant message's container applies `text_ui` (TextSize::Default,
0.875rem); the side-question card's answer container applied nothing and
inherited 1rem. It now applies `text_ui` too.

Test: no GPUI test reads a laid-out text size here; the Xvfb proof is the
check -- before, the same line was 409 px in the card against 358 px in the
thread (Red); after, the two are equal (docs/assets/zeo-batch-0270-2026-11-24
in the hub). The side-question suites still run.
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view/side_question_card.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view/side_question_card.rs
index 8b4a5ba..175eab8 100644
--- a/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view/side_question_card.rs
+++ b/crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view/side_question_card.rs
@@ -253,8 +253,12 @@ impl ThreadView {
                 .into_any_element(),
             SideQuestionState::Answered { markdown, .. } => {
                 let style = MarkdownStyle::themed(MarkdownFont::Agent, window, cx);
+                // The thread's messages take their size from `text_ui` on their container
+                // (`TextSize::Default`, 0.875rem), not from the Markdown style; without it the
+                // answer inherited 1rem and read 8/7 larger (operator ask 6 of 2026-11-23).
                 div()
                     .w_full()
+                    .text_ui(cx)
                     .max_h(px(SIDE_ANSWER_MAX_HEIGHT))
                     .child(
                         div()
